module Core

### Represents a type that a value of `S` converts to: `S.to[Me]()` builds one.
### :typeparam S: The type converted from.
protocol ConvertibleFrom[S]
    ### Builds this type's value from `from`, failing when it does not fit.
    ### :param from: The value to convert.
    ### :returns: The converted value.
    routine Me!(from: S) -> Me

### Converts this value to `T`: `count.to[U8]()`, `text.to[S64]()`. A value that does not fit `T` (or text that
### does not read as one) crashes, and `try x.to[U8]()` recovers it as `none`. Where the surrounding code already
### says the type (`var n: U64 = count.to()`), the type argument can be left out.
### :typeparam T: The type to convert to.
### :returns: This value as a `T`.
### :throws: {IntegerOverflowError} when the value does not fit `T`.
routine N.to![T]() -> T
needs AnyType N
needs T obeys ConvertibleFrom[N]
    return T(from: me)
